# LAW ISOLATION, from the law library (note/project/term/assurance/prove-loop/decision/002-law-library.md): a person's
# view never shows another person's note. Every note the app's `view` computes for the person `person(i, r)` is a
# note of that person, so `view` can neither show a note of someone else nor relabel one as theirs (`owned` reads the
# note's own `whose`).
#
# A project states the law by FUSING this template with its own forms and its view task, and proves the claim it
# makes with a `task isolation` of its own. It may not write the claim itself: `term knit` refuses a claim named
# `isolation` that is not this one (call/code/knit-law.ts). The template is used IN the file that fuses it: `term knit`
# appends this text below a marker at that file's end, because `term hold --report` and the Lean exporter read only a
# file's own templates.
#
#   fuse isolation-law
#     bind state, shelf
#     bind natural, natural
#     bind rank, rank
#     bind person, person
#     bind view, view
#
# THE SHAPE IT READS, whatever the forms are called: `state` is a list with the cases `bare` and `more` (`top`, a
# note, and `rest`), a note has the cases `live` (`at`, `whose`) and `gone` (`at`, `whose`, `by`), `person` is a
# record of `id` (a `natural`) and `rank`, and `view` takes the state and a person to a state.
#
# Its shape is law.tree's `isolation-of-view` in test/assurance/notes, the notes demo, with `owned` from the same file.
# The body is written so it reads the same in a lean file and a longhand one.

tree isolation-law
  take state, like name
  take natural, like name
  take rank, like name
  take person, like name
  take view, like name

  hook fuse
    # every note on the list is owned by `who`, live or gone
    form owned
      head who, like {person}
      head v, like {state}
      case owned-end
        link doer, like {person}
        head
          read doer
        head
          make bare
      case owned-live
        link at, like {natural}
        link w, like {natural}
        link r, like {rank}
        link rest, like {state}
        link rest-owned
          like owned
            head
              make {person}
                bind id, w
                bind rank, r
            head
              read rest
        head
          make {person}
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          make more
            bind top
              make live
                bind at, at
                bind whose, w
            bind rest, rest
      case owned-gone
        link at, like {natural}
        link w, like {natural}
        link r, like {rank}
        link by, like {person}
        link rest, like {state}
        link rest-owned
          like owned
            head
              make {person}
                bind id, w
                bind rank, r
            head
              read rest
        head
          make {person}
            bind id, w
            bind rank, r
        head
          make more
            bind top
              make gone
                bind at, at
                bind whose, w
                bind by, by
            bind rest, rest

    # ISOLATION: every note `view` computes for a person is that person's
    rule isolation
      take s, like {state}
      take i, like {natural}
      take r, like {rank}
      like owned
        head
          make {person}
            bind id, i
            bind rank, r
        head
          call {view}
            read s
            make {person}
              bind id, i
              bind rank, r
